import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.HolomorphicPicardNativeGluingCore

/-!
# Native holomorphic line bundles from genuine unit-valued Čech cocycles

An arbitrary actual open cover and an actual Čech cocycle of the genuine
holomorphic units sheaf produce a native holomorphic complex line bundle.
The section identities are evaluated to prove the transition identities,
and the original holomorphic section proves regularity on each overlap.
The final bundle uses the existing native `VectorBundleCore`, and its
actual local coordinate changes equal the original cocycle values.
-/
